<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aulus Terentius Varro Murena</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aulus Terentius Varro Murena was a Roman general in the early reign of Augustus. In 25 BCE he conquered the Salassi of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aosta">Aosta</a> valley, selling about 36,000 of them into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a>, and founded the colony of Augusta Praetoria, modern Aosta, on their land. He is sometimes identified with the Murena executed for conspiring against Augustus around 22 BCE, but this is disputed.</p></div>
